Pedro is currently a tenure-track assistant professor in the Department of Biostatistics at the University of Pittsburgh School of Public Health.  

He received his PhD in Biostatistics in 2020 working under the guidance of Drs. Naim Rashid and Joseph Ibrahim, where he developed novel statistical methods for cancer genomics.  

After graduation he completed a three-year postdoctoral fellowship under Dr. Gordon Smyth, developing statistical and computational tools for the analysis of RNA-seq data. 
